A||||7||Mach10||Attn Ogre: Aboot your fan mods:||||5||
Z||000000||Mach10||09-01-2001||11:26 AM||||I'm trying to install override switches for my rad and aux fans. I've got all the bits, and some indicator lamps. Looks pretty trick, actually.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>My problem is that I'm reading your instructions for the thermoswitch(sub'ing in a plain on-off pushbutton for the thermal switch) and is says to splice into the white-green wire, and ground it. All I got is a green, a couple of reds, and a few blacks and greys. Am I correct in assuming that green's the one? I can test it myself, but I'd rather leave the insulators as intact as possible...<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Galen||09-01-2001||01:23 PM||||Theres a green&white(I think) somewhere aboot under ya dash. just look hard. Hard Young Grasshooper<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <FONT SIZE="1">under construction</FONT><BR><LI> AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe<FONT SIZE="1"><BR><LI> ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||09-01-2001||01:30 PM||||From the instructions, it appears that the switch would activate the relay beside the headlight directly. There's any number of green-white wires under the dash. I'm interested in the one off the relay. I don't seem to have one. Am I going about this in the wrong way?||||reg||7
Z||000003||theogre||09-01-2001||02:48 PM||||It should be a green wire with a white stripe. <P>In your case, if you have AC you can get that wire on the back of the AC controls.<P>You can also pick it up where is passes thru the firewall.<P>If your all the way up by the relay, it should be the only green wire on the relay. The others should be heavy reds and a thin brown/white.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||09-01-2001||03:16 PM||||Sweet deal! Thanks Ogre! This should be pretty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||12
Z||000005||ka4nkf||09-02-2001||12:27 AM||||I think I am correct, because I just did mine. It is the forth wire on the left from the bottom of the wiring block above the brake pedal that goes thru the firewall. green with white stripe.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||09-02-2001||04:25 AM||||Thanks anyhoo. I just tapped into the line off the AC control wiring harness. It WAS a green-whitestripe wire. Worked flawlessly, until I knocked the pushbutton switch through my backing plate  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>Was relativly trouble free, until I was testing a potential ground, stuck the probe into the cigar lighter, only to discover that someone have stuffed it full of change. ZZZaaap-POOF! And a small blue puff of smoke from my fuse block. My last 25A fuse... ****.<BR>Oh well, at least the dime melted a bit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks for your superb directions, Ogre!||||reg||12
Z||000007||Galen||09-02-2001||06:19 AM||||hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm going to bed..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> to dream about fuses<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <FONT SIZE="1">under construction</FONT><BR><LI> AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe<FONT SIZE="1"><BR><LI> ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558</FONT>||||reg||1
